@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
title Proposed private cache strategy — reuse content, never stale permission
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

actor Caller
rectangle "Owner resolves current account / link / grant\nand intended publication/language/mode" as A
rectangle "Exact scoped cache key\nImmutable content / rendition / input identity" as K
database "Derived private projection / artifact cache\nFreshness, size, invalidation and backend pending" as C
rectangle "Authorized owner rebuild / exact artifact resolution" as R
rectangle "Guarded current delivery admission\nAccurate unavailable/denied state if needed" as D
Caller --> A
A --> K : permitted context
K --> C : lookup exact identity
C --> D : matching usable result
C ..> R : safe miss only
R --> D
D --> Caller : permitted projection / controlled bytes
legend bottom
 A cache hit is not authority or proof of usable bytes; invalidation/refill races need actual synchronization.
 Public static-asset caching is a different classification. No TTL, Redis or CDN is selected.
endlegend
@enduml
